00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:34,605
But this isn't your karaoke, old man,

257
00:14:34,655 --> 00:14:36,760
how long are you going
to keep hogging the mic?

258
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,520
Officer Ryotsu!

259
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:40,020
Y-yes, sir? What is it?

260
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:44,020
Please prepare the children's corner.

261
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:53,260
Good children, everyone,

262
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:58,660
you're small,
so drivers can't see you easily.

263
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,300
Please be careful.

264
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,160
Yes!

265
00:15:02,760 --> 00:15:06,520
That Chief, he's planning to make
a fool of me for his own amusement.

266
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:10,840
When crossing the pedestrian crossing,
raise your hand high and cross properly.

267
00:15:11,860 --> 00:15:12,580
Yes!

268
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:27,460
Waaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

269
00:15:27,460 --> 00:15:28,540
Let's be careful.

270
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:35,080
Next is the case of bicycle accidents,
which are common among elementary school kids.

271
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:38,560
The most common bicycle accident is
getting caught in a truck's wheels.

272
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:40,800
Let's recreate the scene here.

273
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:46,960
Damn it, how ridiculous.

274
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:50,200
What on earth am I doing
dressed up like this?

275
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:53,160
Hey, kids shouldn't say "washi" like that.

276
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:54,620
Kankichi-ku.

277
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:54,780
Grr!

278
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:57,420
Ugh, sorry.

279
00:15:57,420 --> 00:15:59,900
Alright, alright,
in the case of a left turn,

280
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:00,429
Yo!

281
00:16:00,479 --> 00:16:04,920
Bicycles especially need to watch
out for large trucks and such.

282
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:09,160
At intersections like this,
when a large truck turns,

283
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:11,401
due to the inner wheel difference,
this young boy,

284
00:16:11,451 --> 00:16:15,080
There's a risk this boy could
get caught under the rear wheels.

285
00:16:15,080 --> 00:16:19,400
I'm going to demonstrate with this boy now,
so please watch closely.

286
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:22,280
Chief, there's no need to keep
knocking me on the head like that.

287
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:23,340
I'm not the Chief.

288
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:25,320
This is the driver.

289
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:28,120
Pay attention and watch properly,
elementary school kids.

290
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,740
Alright, everyone?

291
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:32,620
Please keep your eyes on this, on this.

292
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:34,720
Now, I'll begin the demonstration.

293
00:16:35,700 --> 00:16:40,860
The inner wheel difference is when the rear
tires swing inward as the vehicle turns.

294
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:44,700
In a situation like this,
it will definitely run over that boy.

295
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:50,440
Damn it, I'm not falling for
the chief's trap that easily!

296
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:51,580
Just watch.

297
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:54,180
Here, the inner wheel difference
kicks in and the boy -

298
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,540
Get out!

299
00:16:56,540 --> 00:17:00,140
That guy dodged on purpose, didn't he?

300
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,780
At this rate, my position will -

301
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:04,420
Go back!

302
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:05,700
Ryotsu, you...

303
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:11,740
That was an example of how
running away might just save you.

304
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:14,860
But if you think you'll get away every time,
you're dead wrong.

305
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:16,680
The next one is the real thing.

306
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,380
Wait there, Ryotsu!

307
00:17:18,380 --> 00:17:20,000
This time, I won't miss.

308
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,460
I'll keep running no matter
how many times it takes.

309
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:25,880
I won't let the chief have his way!

310
00:17:26,620 --> 00:17:27,340
Here I go.

311
00:17:29,340 --> 00:17:33,520
Like this, you also need to be
careful when running alongside a truck.

312
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:37,000
Hey, don't let your bicycle
go faster than the truck!

313
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,600
It's to survive the traffic war, you see.

314
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:44,360
I won't let you escape!

315
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:54,440
Like this, there's no telling when a
truck might come swerving over to crowd you.

316
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:57,060
Please, everyone, be very careful too.

317
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:58,060
Nice!

318
00:17:58,060 --> 00:17:59,360
Stop it!

319
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:04,000
Damn it! The truck jumped and spun right into us,
and you call that crowding?

320
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,280
Boom!

321
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:07,340
It's like a children's fight.

322
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:10,040
That hardly looks like
traffic safety negotiation.

323
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:14,620
Let's follow the rules and survive the
traffic war where anything can happen.

324
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:19,120
Don't go saying "anything can happen," okay?

325
00:18:20,280 --> 00:18:23,680
I'll make you taste the
meaning of those words, Chief.

326
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:29,000
Next up are accidents involving 50cc motorbikes,
which are common among women too.

327
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:33,060
Although they're 50cc scooters,
they can reach quite high speeds,

328
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:35,440
so please make sure you ride safely.

329
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,700
Sorry to keep you waiting.

330
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,440
What?

331
00:18:39,460 --> 00:18:44,260
Chief, you've got to show us a
proper example of safe driving.

332
00:18:44,260 --> 00:18:46,100
What? Fine.

333
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:51,100
I've been waiting for this moment.
Come on, get on, hop on!

334
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:53,380
Ryotsu, you're scheming something,
aren't you?

335
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:58,040
First, straddle the bike while
the kickstand is still down.

336
00:18:58,040 --> 00:19:00,860
And of course,
don't forget to put on your helmet.

337
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:05,320
Before you start the engine and pull away,
check your surroundings carefully.

338
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:40,120
Check behind you!

339
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:46,660
Was this your doing, you bedridden fool?

340
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:55,880
Please, everyone, never drive like this.

341
00:19:57,660 --> 00:20:00,200
Nobody's listening.
They're all staring at Honda.

342
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:02,293
You idiot! Honda,

343
00:20:02,343 --> 00:20:04,620
show us some safe driving!

344
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:05,000
Gah!

345
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:18,680
Now let's test a more dangerous car accident with this ugly doll.
That damn Chief is really out to make a fool of my legs, isn't he.

346
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:28,760
As you can see,
even at just under 20 kilometers an hour,

347
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:31,520
you can see there's considerable damage.

348
00:20:32,060 --> 00:20:33,840
Now, let's speed it up a bit.

349
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:37,480
Let's keep testing how
much that doll can take.

350
00:20:38,260 --> 00:20:40,400
Poor little Ryo-chan doll.

351
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:43,860
It's as if the real me is being beaten up.

352
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:45,960
Ryo-san, sir

353
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:49,000
Are we just going to sit
here and watch in silence?

354
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,140
No way,
this is Kankichi Ryotsu we're talking about.

355
00:20:51,140 --> 00:20:54,240
He's not the type to sit
back and take humiliation.

356
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:58,440
Next, let's run the experiment
at a full 60 kilometers per hour.

357
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:03,560
So, will that doll be able to withstand it?

358
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:06,580
They're only dolls,
but I feel a little guilty about this.

359
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:07,300
Go ahead.

360
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:10,500
Finally!

361
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:10,660
Here it comes!

362
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:15,060
Look! A motorcycle is falling from the sky!

363
00:21:15,620 --> 00:21:19,560
Isn't that what they call a traffic war, where
you never know what's going to happen? Chief!

364
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:23,740
Damn you! You're bent on ruining
this seminar at every turn!

365
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:26,160
Go, Nakagawa!

366
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:26,600
Yes!

367
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:38,340
What are you dawdling for!
Can't you catch up?

368
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:41,560
It's no good!
Like this, the bikes have the advantage!

369
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:47,440
What are you doing! Move forward already!

370
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:50,460
It's no good!
There's oil spread across the road,

371
00:21:50,510 --> 00:21:53,280
and we can't go forward or turn!

372
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:54,120
What the hell!

373
00:21:56,820 --> 00:22:03,640
Look behind you! Traffic wars are scary, aren't they!
Oil gets spread on the road out of nowhere, doesn't it!

374
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:03,880
Hey...

375
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:17,540
Alright, finish it off quickly! Are you really sure about this?
You upstart, what are you scared of? If you're going to do it, go all the way!

376
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:19,640
Alright, let's pull off something big!

377
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:20,380
Me!

378
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:25,320
Nooo!

379
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:26,580
Let's kill them!

380
00:22:32,260 --> 00:22:33,800
What's with those guys!

381
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:35,100
Ryo-chan!

382
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:37,480
Hey! Is this even allowed!

383
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:39,960
What a messy, pathetic sight

384
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:41,260
Let's go!

385
00:22:42,660 --> 00:22:46,300
How cool!

386
00:22:48,060 --> 00:22:49,780
They're loving it, they're loving it!

387
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,980
Yeah! Double peace signs
and we're totally killing it!

388
00:22:56,560 --> 00:23:00,380
See that? Put in the effort and it works out.
That's the basic rule of the world.

389
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:03,060
Don't just say "that's the rule," you idiot!

390
00:23:06,540 --> 00:23:07,340
No way!

391
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:12,420
Come on! The safety seminar isn't over yet!

392
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:13,620
What's going on here?

393
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:22,920
Everyone, thank you for your hard
work during today's long seminar.

394
00:23:22,920 --> 00:23:25,320
We will now perform the final demonstration.

395
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:30,440
Two police officers prepared to risk
everything will attempt a car-to-car shock test.

396
00:23:30,860 --> 00:23:33,360
Please, everyone, do not try to copy this.

397
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:33,780
Well then,

398
00:23:34,280 --> 00:23:37,440
Go on, Nakagawa, charge in with
everything you've got in the Zakkiro!

399
00:23:37,840 --> 00:23:38,660
Is that really all right?

400
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:40,360
Carmar, go for it!

401
00:23:43,720 --> 00:23:45,980
Bring out the Chief!

402
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:47,880
Sorry, Chief!

403
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:48,620
Please stop, okay?

404
00:23:49,020 --> 00:23:51,720
We're not dummy dolls, you know.

405
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:07,080
Yay! Tomorrow's party
is at Nakagawa's house!

406
00:24:07,080 --> 00:24:10,180
Apparently it's a birthday party for
the prince of the Bookshelf Kingdom.

407
00:24:10,180 --> 00:24:11,660
That's Nakagawa's house, for sure.

408
00:24:11,660 --> 00:24:13,960
There must be mountains of food!

409
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:17,860
Alright, starting today I won't eat
a thing and I'll keep my stomach empty.

410
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:20,980
Next time:
a look at Nakagawa's otaku collection!

411
00:24:20,980 --> 00:24:21,840
Thanks, see you then.

412
00:24:32,300 --> 00:24:36,700
Always keep smiling, okay?

413
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:40,920
Even when something outrageous happens,

414
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:45,400
keep smiling sweetly, okay?

415
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:50,620
Just step out with a casual face.

416
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:57,480
Hey, smile for me. It's not your fault.

417
00:24:58,820 --> 00:25:05,780
Hey, smile for me,
like you were a moment ago.

418
00:25:05,780 --> 00:25:16,660
Always keep smiling.
A woman who's too serious isn't beautiful.

419
00:25:16,660 --> 00:25:21,380
You should smile right away.

420
00:25:22,620 --> 00:25:25,840
Unless you're a child.

